be dropped with a batch being committed: `stageProposedOps` waits for checkout's `commitsLanded()` — no commit running, and a landed one applied by the replica (`replicaSettled()`) and taken in by the store — before it stages its list through `emitMany`; the DiffDrawer stays committing and undismissable (Commit/Cancel disabled, no close button, Escape and outside clicks ignored) through the POST and, on a landed commit, until checkout's `commitApplied()` resolves — `commitsLanded()` (while `ready`, once the replica has applied the answer), or the replica `off`/`server`/`failed` — then closes (a `failed` replica keeps the answer and the rebuilt one applies it on its first drain, under the overlay; waiting on in `failed` would also wait on edits and mirror reads held until then; a rebind that freezes the replica before the answer is applied keeps it queued until adoption, the committed batches out of the readers and an update that would merge into one of them deferred meanwhile); `Cmd/Ctrl+S` opens no drawer while `isReplicaBlocked()`; a refused commit frees it at once, and on the legacy side `commitApplied()` is `null` and it closes when the POST answers. `discardConflict(batchId)` drops a parked batch and releases the leases its ops needed that no remaining staged op needs; the element discards read the remaining ops once the unstage has landed, and keep every lease while the staged list is unreadable. `DiffDrawer` renders `getStagedConflicts()` as a section of its own under the entity rows (`data-testid="staged-conflicts"`, headed `N staged edits no longer apply` — always plural — one row per parked batch, `conflict-row-<batchId>`, each op summarised like an entity row plus the engine's `error.detail` verbatim and a ghost Discard calling `discardConflict`), outside its `total` and never part of a commit; `[]` on the legacy side, so the section never renders there. The facade's `emitMany`, `stagedSettled`, `getStagedBatchIds`, `getStagedConflicts`, `revertConflict`,